"Armament-granted skill economy: a 1-handed weapon grants 3 skills, a 2-handed grants 6, and two of the SAME weapon grant the base 3 plus a bonus 3 that use both together (dual-wield). Add status-effect actions for players AND enemies: e.g. Raise Shield (+2 defense for 2 rounds), On Guard with a sword (+1 defense for 3 turns). Axes and shields must NOT natively grant buffs as strong as raising attack/defense; instead axes get a heavy attack that LOWERS the user's own defense for 1 round (most pronounced on a 2-handed large axe). Also give weak enemies some purely time-wasting actions (they sometimes squander a turn) for difficulty texture. Depends on the status-effect system and the armament->action derivation."